cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PrideShield: Multimodal Detection of Anti-LGBTQ+ Hate Speech in Memes"
message: "If you use this software or reference this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ankush
    family-names: Singh
    email: ankush.singh1802@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/Vermillion-1/PrideShield"
abstract: >-
  A multimodal classification pipeline for detecting anti-LGBTQ+ hate speech in
  internet memes, combining OpenAI CLIP visual/text embeddings with an MLP
  classification head, benchmarked against a BERT text-only baseline. Includes
  the full data pipeline: multi-platform collection, OCR extraction and
  correction, perceptual deduplication, and dual-annotator label reconciliation.
keywords:
  - multimodal-learning
  - hate-speech-detection
  - CLIP
  - content-moderation
  - computer-vision
  - natural-language-processing
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: 2025-05-17
